    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by [ a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
            crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "lace, a string or cord serving to draw together opposite edges of clothing (bodices, stays, boots, shoes) by being passed through eyelet-holes or over hooks and pulled tight (OED s.v. lace n. 3); here measured in gross — so not lace n. 6 (the openwork fabric, measured in yards). Made of thread, leather, hair, worsted or caddis. For gold/silver decorative braid see passemain; see also point, scholas (shoelaces), aglett." ;
            crm:P2_has_type aat:300435416 ] ;
